WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.000
-Our first guest tonight,

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.467
hosts Sunday TODAY with
Willie Geist

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.667
Sunday mornings on NBC.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.400
He also co-hosts
Morning Joe,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.200
weekday mornings on MSNBC.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.067
Please welcome back to the show
Willie Geist, everybody.

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:12.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:21.868
♪♪

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:31.200
♪♪

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.734
Nice to have you back, man.
-Hey man. How are you?

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:34.634
Good. You shared
a very nice moment

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.968
with me as we
were walking out.

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:37.968
You said your makeup
was also very bad during COVID.

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:39.067
-I was watching the monologue.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.901
My first interview
I did during COVID.

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:44.334
I had people call me after
and saying prayers up.

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:45.334
You have COVID.

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:46.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.200
-That's how bad you looked.
-That's how bad it was.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.968
And I, like you, appreciate our
makeup artist so much more.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:53.133
-Yes. Well,
you also took advantage

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.767
of both makeup and wardrobe

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:57.367
because the Halloween
on The TODAY Show,

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:58.701
this is a tradition.

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:00.534
This is the highest bar.
I'm going to --

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:03.234
This is I'm not just being
a Homer NBC guy.

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:04.934
The costumes on
The TODAY Show

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:06.300
are other level.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.501
-Well, here's our secret.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.167
We have an amazing team
at The TODAY Show,

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.467
plus a group
you know well --

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:15.367
the SNL costume,
hair, makeup, wardrobe,

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:17.601
the wigs,
the whole show, so.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.467
-Two years ago, we actually
had you on this same day,

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:20.634
two years ago,
you've been Tom Brady.

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:22.567
You upped your game
this year, my friend.

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:25.400
You were Harry Styles.
-I was Harry Styles. Yeah.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.901
-And and there --
there's a photo

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:27.968
of Harry Styles right there.

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.400
And you're just really...

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:31.734
...really going for it.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:32.834
-That angle.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:35.868
-This is, uh...

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.701
-Oh, wow. Wow.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.667
-This is a tall
Harry Styles.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:40.901
-[ Laughing ] So tall.
-So tall.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.934
-Tall and not quite as lean
as Harry Styles.

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:46.000
-Now, were your colleagues
impressed?

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.934
Do you get feedback
when you show up on set

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.133
from the other
TODAY show team?

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:50.634
-It's a very supportive
environment

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.167
because everybody's putting
themselves out there.

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:53.501
-And a lot of times when you're
putting it out there

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:56.000
on The TODAY Show,
that out there is outside.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.400
-Outside.
-A lot of the show is outside.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.400
-It is.
-It is not the summer.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.667
-No, it's not the summer.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.567
So you first of all,
we get out there

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:04.534
at 5:00 a.m. to rehearse.
-Yeah.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.267
-And then the big show
is about 8:00.

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:07.267
So it's, you know.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:08.801
It's late October.
-Yeah.

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:11.067
-It's 40 degrees
or something like that.

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:13.167
I have a skintight jumpsuit on

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:15.000
with diagonal stripes.
-Yeah.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.167
-In the commercial break,

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:19.133
[Laughing] Al Roker,
Al Roker came up to me

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.501
and started reading
the weather on my body.

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:22.501
And by that
I mean he goes,

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:24.634
"Ooh, it's awfully
chilly up here."

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:26.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:30.133
And then he says, "And
unseasonably cool down here."

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:31.934
-How dare he.
How dare he.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.634
-Isn't that mean?
-Meteorology comedy, it's done.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.234
-Yeah, at work, it's a cliche.
-You also, you --

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.567
Look, this wasn't just costume,
you know,

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:40.267
again, a lot of the best people

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.000
put their best
into the way you looked.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.334
You then matched that effort
with your dance moves.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.501
Can we -- Can we talk
a little over this video

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.067
of what you're having here?
-Yes, let's see what you have.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.033
Oh, Gosh.
-I mean, that's really good.

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.334
You're lip-synching.
-Is it?

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:54.267
-That's the lip-synching part.
So, Harry Styles...

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:55.901
-There's a real good
Harry Styles move right here

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:57.033
at the end that I.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.601
-Yeah. You know
I see it on playback.

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:00.901
-There it is.

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:03.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.634
There it is.

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:07.133
-Really? Yeah?

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:09.734
I don't know.

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:11.934
I spent a lot of time
in the days

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:14.434
leading up
to Halloween on YouTube

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:17.334
with Harry Styles dance moves,
to the point my kids are like,

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:20.434
"Dad, are you still watching
Harry Styles dance?"

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:23.267
And I pulled out, I think,
he has three big moves.

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:25.634
First, we're just going
big energy like a fist pump.

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:26.901
-Yeah, he does the fist pump.

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:28.467
-And then on this song,
as it was,

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:31.667
I noticed he does a big
like a reverse windmill thing.

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:33.534
-Yeah.
-So that's number two.

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:37.000
And then the last one you saw
there was big on Instagram

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.601
I think, where he does like
he's in here a little bit

00:03:39.601 --> 00:03:40.901
and he's leaned back.

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:43.634
And the crowd screams.
-I accidentally watched it once.

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:45.200
-Accidentally.
-And I feel like the algorithm

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.567
is like, hey,
you want to see that every day?

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:47.634
-I know.

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.033
Imagine me.
-Yeah.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.501
-I spent two days watching.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:51.767
the FBI's going
to seize my computer.

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:52.767
-I feel like for our
professional job

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:53.934
sometimes we have
to watch stuff.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.667
I once a month,
I'd like to have a meeting

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:57.033
with the algorithm people
and be like,

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:58.267
"Hey, that's not me."

00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:00.267
-No, that was for work.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:02.767
-That was a thing for work.
-Yes, clear all.

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:05.167
-And, yeah, every time
I'm going to watch it.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:07.667
But that doesn't mean I want you
to keep giving it to me.

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:09.100
-That's the thing.
That's the thing.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.968
You reject it
and then you just lean into it.

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:12.501
-Yeah.
-You just accept that you can't.

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:15.067
-Like, I guess I am
who you are telling me I am.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:16.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.200
I mean, every now and then,
because this one did, I think,

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.367
maybe go a little bit
more viral than a normal

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:22.801
"TODAY Show" segment.
-Yeah.

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:25.167
Did you hear from anybody
who you realize maybe isn't

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:27.033
watching the show every day,
but saw it on social media?

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:30.100
-Oh, my gosh, I -- So my
daughter had a game yesterday.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.000
She plays field hockey.
We go to the visiting field,

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.667
which means I don't know
the parents.

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:38.133
I walk in, walk past
a group of moms

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:40.567
and they all go,
"Hi, Harry." Yeah.

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:41.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.601
And I was like,
oh, this is my legacy.

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:44.634
Yeah, this is it.

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:45.734
-You did all this.
-This is how...

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:47.234
-All this work
and that's your legacy.

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:49.868
-It's been a long road and this
is all I'll be remembered for.

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:52.200
-Well, I do want to talk
to you about the other stuff

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.734
I think you should be
remembered for.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:56.133
We'll be right back with more
from our friend Willie Geist.

